**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The session's library: the library's stores overlaid with the kit's read-only snapshots, so the kit opens on any machine (001 §E 'So the kit opens on any machine', 'missing locally → the snapshot read-only', 'divergence → … the kit keeps its snapshot'; the S4.2 brief: the session's library is the database view overlaid with the kit's read-only snapshot entries, a LibraryProxy composition). In `KitLibrary.fs`, each type and member documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.2: (1) `EntryReplacement = { incoming : LibraryEntryId; held : LibraryEntryEnvelope }` is a kit entry the user re-bound to a held entry ('use my Si instead', 001 §B). `KitLibraryOverlay = { snapshots : LibraryEntryEnvelope list; replacements : EntryReplacement list }`. `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitLibraryStores = { library : LibraryProxy; materials : MaterialProxy; samples : SampleProxy; categories : CategoryProxy }` is the library stores a constructor session reads. (2) `member this.openOverlay (rebindings : EntryRebinding list) : Result<KitLibraryOverlay, KitLibraryError>` on `KitLibraryContext` lists the kit's snapshots and reads each re-binding's held entry through `imports.proxy.tryLatestEnvelope rebinding.held`; one that is not held is `UnheldEntryErr`. The re-bindings are the `ImportOutcome.rebindings` of a confirmed resolution (step 143). It writes nothing. (3) The overlay rule, one member per store, as type extensions after the record: `type LibraryProxy with member this.overlaidWith (overlay : KitLibraryOverlay) : LibraryProxy`, and the same member on `MaterialProxy`, `SampleProxy` and `CategoryProxy`. Every write field passes through to the store unchanged. A read of one version of an entry (`resolveVersion`) answers the held entry for a replaced entry; otherwise the kit's snapshot of that version when the kit holds one, so a divergent version is the kit's (001 §E); otherwise the store's. A read by id (`tryGetMaterial`, `tryGetSample`, `tryGetEntry`) answers the held entry for a replaced entry; otherwise the store's; otherwise the kit's highest-version snapshot of the id. Listings: `LibraryProxy.entriesForKind` answers the store's entries followed by the kit's snapshot-only entries offered for the kind (`LibraryEntry.forKinds`), one per id at its highest version, with a replaced or store-held id left out. `libraryTrees` is `[ LibraryTree.byKind <those entries> ]` (step 47), over the five kinds step 47 names, distinct by id. `CategoryProxy.listCategories` answers the store's categories followed by the kit's snapshot-only ones. `listMaterials`, `searchMaterials`, `listSamples` and `searchSamples` pass through, because the Materials and Library windows show the library (001 §F). A snapshot reaches a domain value only through step 25's decoders, so no entry id becomes a kind's id anywhere else. A decoder's refusal is the store's own unavailable case (`LibraryUnavailableErr`, `MaterialStoreUnavailableErr`, `SampleStoreUnavailableErr`, `CategoryStoreUnavailableErr`, steps 69-79), naming the snapshot and the refusal's `describe`. (4) `member this.overlaidWith (overlay : KitLibraryOverlay) : KitLibraryStores` on `KitLibraryStores` overlays each of its four stores. No cache, write-back or other member is added. Tests, new facts in `KitLibraryTests`. `a kit opened against an empty library resolves every entry from its snapshots`: a kit is snapshotted (step 139) from the Built-in library with the references of the multilayer sample and of the 600 nm source preset. It is then opened read-only by a second proxy over the same folder, in a second context over EMPTY in-memory stores and seam (`CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, step 95), whose `KitLibraryStores` hold a live library composed over those stores as `LibraryProxyTests` composes one (step 78). `resolveSnapshots` answers `EntryIdNotHeld` for every snapshot. Over `openOverlay []`, every snapshot resolves, each equal to its catalogue value: the sample through `samples.resolveVersion` and `library.tryGetEntry`, each material version through `materials.resolveVersion`, each category through `categories.listCategories`, and the preset through `library.tryGetEntry` and `entriesForKind LightSource`. `the session resolves a divergent version to the kit's snapshot`: over the Built-in library, for a kit holding Silicon at version 1 with another description, `materials.resolveVersion` of Silicon at version 1 answers the kit's description, and `tryGetMaterial` of Silicon answers the library's latest. `a re-bound entry resolves to the held entry`: over the Built-in library, a test-local sample the kit alone holds, re-bound to `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` through `openOverlay`, resolves to the multilayer through `samples.tryGetSample` and `library.tryGetEntry`, and `entriesForKind Sample` offers no entry of the kit sample's id. `the overlay passes every write to the library and never lists a kit entry in it`: `samples.saveSample` of a new sample through the overlaid stores holds it in the underlying store, and no listing of the underlying stores answers a kit entry.

**Acceptance.** After the overlay lands, `KitLibraryStores.overlaidWith` MUST answer every kit snapshot the library lacks read-only, the kit's copy of a divergent version and the held entry for a re-bound one, passing every write to the library; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit opened against an empty library resolves every entry from its snapshots`, `the session resolves a divergent version to the kit's snapshot`, `a re-bound entry resolves to the held entry`, `the overlay passes every write to the library and never lists a kit entry in it`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.
